# Update FlySWATTER app

Whenever the user asks to update the app (e.g. "update the app", "pull the latest", "get the newest version", "rebuild with latest"), run this flow immediately:

1. `git pull` from the repo remote.
2. Rebuild for the current OS:
   - macOS: `bash BATCH_SCRIPTS/build_flyswatter_mac_app.sh`
   - Windows: `powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File BATCH_SCRIPTS\build_flyswatter_windows_exe.ps1`
3. Report the built artifact path (`FlySWATTER.app` or `FlySWATTER.exe`) and remind them to quit any running instance before opening the new build.

If the macOS script fails on `xattr` under `.git`, complete the PyInstaller build and copy steps manually instead of stopping.
